tddlog, baselines branch

The source code of tddlog is licensed under the Apache License 2.0
(LICENSE). This branch, the main branch plus the code and programs that
reproduce the published comparisons, also holds copies of third-party
programs and data, under their own terms:

- tests/problog: programs from ProbLog's system test suite
  (https://github.com/ML-KULeuven/problog, test/*.pl), Apache License 2.0.
- data/cplint: example and dataset files from cplint
  (https://github.com/friguzzi/cplint) and cplint_datasets
  (https://github.com/friguzzi/cplint_datasets), Artistic License 2.0.
- data/dice: the baseline programs of Dice
  (https://github.com/SHoltzen/dice, benchmarks/baselines/), Apache
  License 2.0.
- examples/asia.net and examples/cancer.net: two Bayesian networks
  written out from their publications (Lauritzen and Spiegelhalter, 1988;
  Korb and Nicholson, 2004), under the Apache License 2.0 with the rest.

The benchmarks' other Bayesian networks, of the bnlearn repository
(https://www.bnlearn.com/bnrepository/), are not in the repository, as no
license for redistributing them is established: data/fetch.txt names
where each is downloaded (ProbLog's copies, and bnlearn for munin1 to
munin4) and its SHA-256.
- data/alea: benchmark programs of the papers on Alea.jl
  (https://github.com/Tractables/Alea.jl) and of a paper that compares
  with it: arith, hybit and bitblast under the Apache License 2.0, pluck
  under CC-BY-4.0 (the artifact's record). And programs of other papers
  written in Alea.jl, each directory's README citing its source:
  fairsquare, from FairSquare (https://github.com/sedrews/fairsquare),
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2017 Samuel Drews, data/alea/fairsquare/LICENSE
  its text; sppl, from SPPL (https://github.com/probsys/sppl), Apache
  License 2.0; psi, from PSI (https://github.com/eth-sri/psi), Boost
  Software License 1.0, data/alea/psi/LICENSE its text; genfer, from
  Genfer (https://github.com/fzaiser/genfer), MIT License, Copyright (c)
  2023 Fabian Zaiser, data/alea/genfer/LICENSE its text; gubpi and wmi,
  written for tddlog from the papers they cite, under the Apache License
  2.0 with the rest.
- data/hybit: the Stan, WebPPL and Psi programs of the artifact of
  Garg, Holtzen, Van den Broeck and Millstein, "Bit Blasting Probabilistic
  Programs", PLDI 2024 (https://github.com/Tractables/Alea.jl, branch
  hybit), Apache License 2.0; psi/cobs holds rewrites of three of them.
- scripts/samplers/webppl-package-lock.json pins the npm packages of
  WebPPL (MIT) that install_webppl.sh installs; no package is copied.
- data/geni: programs from the artifact of Li and Zhang, "Compiling with
  Generating Functions", ICFP 2025
  (https://github.com/geni-icfp25-ae/geni-icfp25-ae), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2025 Jianlin Li, Oghenevwogaga Ebresafe; data/geni/LICENSE
  holds its text.
- data/nodice: programs from the artifact of Gürtler and Kaminski,
  "noDice", OOPSLA 2026 (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.18739789), record under
  CC-BY-4.0, its repository under the Apache License 2.0.
- data/roulette: programs from the artifact of Moy et al., "Roulette",
  PLDI 2025 (Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.15253254), CC-BY-4.0, from
  https://github.com/camoy/roulette (Apache License 2.0).

Each directory's README gives the source and commit of its files.
